{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c3b93b4de6d03c48","type":"text","text":"Act as an expert in validating ideas for youtube videos.\n\nBased on {{[topic]}} and {{notes}}, answer ONLY the following questions briefly and succinctly in 1-2 sentences.\n1. What is one key takeaway for this video? (one sentence to describe the video)\n2. Why does this video need to exist? (why am I making this video?)","x":200,"y":56,"width":760,"height":304,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"6dfddd82824a3bdf","type":"text","text":"","x":200,"y":440,"width":800,"height":160,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"c62aa7c5b372c1d5","type":"text","text":"Based on {{[topic]}}, {{notes}}, and {{value}} answer the following questions for {{[[Synthbrain/01 - 🎥 Commercial Hub/Youtube Style Guide (Goda)]]}}. Output in a markdown table like below.\n\n| Idea | Thumbnail | What's big/significant about it? | What's easy/useful? | What's new/what can you learn? | Why am I credible to talk about this? |\n| ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- | ---- |\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |","x":100,"y":720,"width":1020,"height":443,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"a71acf90ad644ca6","type":"text","text":"Expectations and Questions\nBased on {{[topic]}}, {{notes}}, {{value}}, and [questions] fill out the below table for {{[[Synthbrain/01 - 🎥 Commercial Hub/Youtube Style Guide (Goda)]]. Output in a markdown table like below.\n\n| Question | Importance | Answer |\n| ---- | ---- | ---- |\n|  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |\n|  |  |  |","x":415,"y":1640,"width":545,"height":360,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"9bd6d9d432dbe32d","type":"text","text":"| Act 1 (set up/conflict/problem)                                                  | Act 2 (Confrontation/problem development)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                   | Act 3 (Resolution)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                       |\n|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Note-taking has become chaotic and disorganized. People are overwhelmed by the volume of information they need to handle.                                               | Introduce Obsidian as a hub for managing knowledge. Detail the problems individuals face with organizing notes. Present the Obsidian Community Plugins as an innovative solution.                                                                                              | Show the transformative effect of using Obsidian plugins on note-taking practices. Viewers learn how to streamline their workflow, manage information efficiently, and integrate new methods of note organization using these plugins, ultimately improving productivity and creativity.    |\n| Many people's digital lives are cluttered, leading to inefficiencies and stress.                                       | Discuss the challenges of managing files across different platforms and devices. Highlight the lack of a coherent system that seamlessly integrates all aspects of digital life.                                                                                              | Demonstrate how Obsidian and its community plugins can centralize and organize digital files, providing a single point of reference for documents, notes, and data, making retrieval and management more straightforward and less time-consuming.                                 |\n| Project teams struggle with collaboration and managing collective knowledge effectively.                             | Explore common collaboration tools and their limitations. Deep dive into issues coordinating team efforts, information siloing, and inefficient project management due to poor note-taking and documentation practices.                                                      | Showcase how Obsidian can empower teams to centralize knowledge, facilitate better communication, and streamline project management. Illustrate successful collaboration using plugins designed to synchronize teamwork within Obsidian's framework.                           |\n| Students and life-long learners need to process and recall large amounts of information but struggle to find a reliable method. | Outline traditional note-taking methods and their shortcomings in supporting complex learning. Examine the cognitive burden of managing educational material without the right tools.                                                                                           | Reveal Obsidian's capability to support advanced learning techniques, e.g., spaced repetition, and interlinking concepts, using community plugins. Demonstrate how these methods promote better information retention and recall, streamlining the learning process.              |\n| Developers require a specialized approach to integrate coding practices with knowledge management.                | Address the complexity of documentation and note-taking for software development. Challenge the fragmented nature of coding resources and knowledge spread across various platforms.                                                                                            | Present a tailored walkthrough of how Obsidian handles code snippets, project documentation, and resource management. Introduce plugins that make this integration natural for developers, enhancing their workflow significantly.                                         |\n| Content creators and writers need a way to harness creativity and manage their content efficiently.               | Illustrate the overwhelm that comes with managing a content creation process without a structured system. Highlight the limitations of existing productivity and note-taking apps in fostering creativity and content organization.                                          | Teach how Obsidian's plugins can be a game-changer for content creators, offering tools for brainstorming, outlining, and interlinking ideas. Show workflows that help transform sporadic thoughts into structured outputs that fuel creativity and streamline content production. |\n\n### Value\n\"By the end of the video on 'Transforming Note-Taking with Obsidian Community Plugins,' viewers should clearly understand that their note-taking and knowledge management can be exponentially improved through innovative plugins, with Obsidian acting as the central hub for ideas and information.\"\n\n### Comment Goals\nThe most fantastic comment would be:\n\"I never realized note-taking could be this seamless and intuitive. Obsidian's plugins, as you've introduced them, are life-changing. Your clear guidance on setup and usage has taken my productivity to new heights – it's like these plugins were the missing pieces of my workflow puzzle. Thanks to your insights, I'm now handling my notes like a pro and connecting ideas with ease. This isn't just a video; it's a blueprint to mastering personal knowledge management!\"\n\n### Audience Expectations and Questions\nAudience expectations include learning hands-on strategies to tackle note chaos, expecting detailed demonstrations of plugin capabilities, and walkthroughs on improving knowledge management practices.\n\nAudience questions could be:\n- \"How can Obsidian plugins directly address my daily note-taking frustrations?\"\n- \"Are these plugins easy to install and use for someone not tech-savvy?\"\n- \"What makes Obsidian's plugins stand out from typical note-taking apps?\"\n- \"How can integrating these plugins into my routine improve my overall productivity and idea management?\"","x":1312,"y":1952,"width":1040,"height":568,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"5139e36e28e88303","type":"text","text":"Based on {{[topic]}}, {{notes}}, and {{value}} create the story arc for {{[[Synthbrain/01 - 🎥 Commercial Hub/Youtube Style Guide (Goda)]]}}. Output in a markdown table like below.\n\n| Act 1 (set up/conflict/problem) | Act 2 (Confrontation/problem development) | Act 3 (Resolution) |\n| ---- | ---- | ---- |\n|  |  |  |","x":1312,"y":1520,"width":1040,"height":339,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"973c38624fd4ddcb","type":"text","text":"Unfortunately, your request is unclear as the provided placeholders (e.g., {{notes}}, {{value}}, and [questions]) do not correspond with any specific context or details that I can reference to generate a markdown table with content about the \"Youtube Style Guide (Goda)\" and its relation to Obsidian Community Plugins.\n\nTo generate a table as requested, I would need more information about the Youtube Style Guide (Goda) and how it relates to the Obsidian Community Plugins, as well as any particular questions, their level of importance, and corresponding answers that you wish to include in the table.\n\nIf you could provide context, real data, or sample content for each of the placeholders and questions, I could then help you create a markdown table with the appropriate information.\n\nFor instance, you might be asking for a table like this:\n\n| Question                                                                | Importance | Answer                                                   |\n| ----------------------------------------------------------------------- | ---------- | -------------------------------------------------------- |\n| What is the purpose of the Youtube Style Guide (Goda) in relation to Obsidian? | High       | To ensure consistency in video content about Obsidian.   |\n| Which Obsidian Community Plugins are recommended in the style guide?    | Medium     | The guide might recommend popular plugins like Calendar and Templater. |\n| How often should the style guide be updated?                           | Low        | Periodic review, such as annually or with major updates to Obsidian. |\n| Are there any formatting requirements for video titles or descriptions?| High       | Yes, the guide stipulates specific formatting rules for titles and descriptions to enhance SEO and viewer readability. |\n\nPlease provide additional information or clarify your request so I can assist you accordingly.","x":415,"y":2136,"width":545,"height":384,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"3ca92ccf39464fca","type":"text","text":"| Idea                                                                                      | Thumbnail                                                                                                                                                                                                                                  | What's big/significant about it?                                                                  | What's easy/useful?                                                                                                | What's new/what can you learn?                                                                            | Why am I credible to talk about this?                                                                          |\n|-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Obsidian Plugins - Transform Your Note-Taking Game!                                        |                                                    | Demonstrating a powerful way to connect ideas and enhance note organization through software.     | Obsidian is a widely accessible tool, plugins can be installed with ease improving the note-taking experience. | Introducing the latest community plugins that can streamline productivity and knowledge management.           | I've extensively used Obsidian and its plugins to optimize my own note-taking system.                           |\n| Boost Productivity with Obsidian: Calendar & Speech-to-Text Plugins                        | The thumbnail shows a calendar with colorful task icons on one side and a microphone with sound waves on the other, on a soft yellow background.                                                                                           | Focuses on organizing tasks more efficiently and utilizing cutting-edge speech-to-text technology. | Direct demonstration of how to integrate these plugins into daily workflow.                                    | Highlighting new plugins in Obsidian's ecosystem that leverage calendar management and speech recognition.    | As a power user of Obsidian, I regularly explore and implement productivity-enhancing tools and share insights. |\n| Unleashing Creativity with Mind Mapping in Obsidian                                        | An image of a vibrant mind map structure with various node labels is shown on the thumbnail. The overall color vibe is bright and energetic, with a combination of orange and teal elements.                                                   | Showcasing the significance of visual idea arrangement and brainstorming within notes.             | Easy-to-understand concept of using mind maps for planning and creative thinking.                              | Learn how to use the newest mind mapping plugins to visualize information inside Obsidian.                     | I've created complex mind maps within Obsidian for personal and professional projects, witnessing their impact. |\n| Organize Your Digital Life: File Management with Obsidian                                  | Thumbnail includes visuals of neatly organized file icons branching off from the central Obsidian logo. The color scheme is professional, with muted blues and greens providing a sense of calm organization.                                  | Addressing the challenge of digital file clutter and providing a scalable solution.                | Explains the simplicity of managing and navigating files within one application.                               | Cover the latest techniques and plugins for optimal file organization in Obsidian.                             | My expertise in digital organization has helped many adopt cleaner and more efficient file management systems. |\n| Take Charge of Your Learning: Advanced Note-Taking Techniques with Obsidian                | Thumbnail features a person in \"eureka\" moment with a lightbulb overhead, surrounded by note-themed icons. The background has a gradient of intellectual, serious colors like maroon blending into a navy blue.                                 | It signifies the importance of effective learning and memory retention through advanced techniques. | Offers practical steps and tools within Obsidian to enhance learning processes.                               | Introduces unique methodologies and plugins that revolutionize the way we take notes.                          | With years of experience in educational technologies, I bring a wealth of knowledge on effective note-taking.   |\n| Collaborate and Conquer: Team Project Management in Obsidian                               | A thumbnail with visuals representing team collaboration, such as linked avatars around a shared project timeline. The color scheme is friendly, implying a collaborative environment with green for growth and yellow for energy and creativity. | Tackles the challenge of managing team projects seamlessly.                                      | Highlights the ease of using Obsidian for team project tracking and collaboration.                            | Showcasing the latest collaborative plugins that integrate with Obsidian workflows.                            | As a project manager, I've led teams using Obsidian to coordinate complex projects successfully.              |\n| From Chaos to Clarity: Taming Your Thoughts with Daily Notes in Obsidian                   | Thumbnail depicts a chaotic scribble turning into a neat tick-marked checklist, symbolizing the transformation from disorganized thoughts to structured ideas. The color theme is calming shades of blue, suggesting clarity of thought.           | Emphasizes the mental clarity and organizational benefits of daily note-taking practices.         | Daily notes are a simple, effective habit that can be easily adopted with Obsidian.                            | Viewers can learn evolving practices and plugin developments in daily logging and reflection.                  | My daily note practice in Obsidian has been a cornerstone of my personal and professional discipline.          |\n| Coding & Knowledge Management: A Developer's Guide to Obsi                             | A thumbnail showing code snippets branching from the Obsidian logo, creating a sense of integration between coding and note-taking, set against a sleek dark matrix-style background.                                                          | Combines the worlds of software development and knowledge management.                            | Targeted at developers, showcasing how Obsidian can fit into a technical workflow.                            | Introducing plugins and features that cater to code-oriented note-taking and documentation.                    | As a developer, I've utilized Obsidian to manage complex developmental documentation and personal notes.      |","x":90,"y":1240,"width":1040,"height":280,"color":"6"},
